   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "31507bf1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Wrong data types are silent killers — your aggregations give wrong results and you don't know why."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9233e5f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Basic Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "8c8bb1ad",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasciencedojo/datasets/master/titanic.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(url)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e9f56229",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Check current types"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "5c73d3fc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "PassengerId      int64\n",
       "Survived         int64\n",
       "Pclass           int64\n",
       "Name               str\n",
       "Sex                str\n",
       "Age            float64\n",
       "SibSp            int64\n",
       "Parch            int64\n",
       "Ticket             str\n",
       "Fare           float64\n",
       "Cabin              str\n",
       "Embarked           str\n",
       "dtype: object"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 5,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df.dtypes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "42da481e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# --- Convert to numeric ---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5bf04b4d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"Age\"] = df[\"Age\"].astype(int)       # float → int (only if no nulls remain)\n",
    "df[\"Fare\"] = df[\"Fare\"].astype(float)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "996dd6b9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "When a numeric column has dirty values mixed in (e.g. \"35abc\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "84aa4e9a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "astype() will crash — use pd.to_numeric with errors=\"coerce\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "1c73b64a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"Age\"] = pd.to_numeric(df[\"Age\"] , errors=\"coerce\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5808a5b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\"coerce\" turns unparseable values into NaN instead of crashing\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9cc1eefc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "You can then handle those NaNs with fillna()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d4f4aa45",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# --- Convert to datetime ---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "68ffa45a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"date\"])\n",
    "df[\"date\"] = pd.datetime(df[\"date\"] , format=\"%Y-%m-%d\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "763807f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Once it's datetime, you can extract parts"
   ]
  },
  {
